---
title: Disclosure Gate — Page Seal State Machine
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR

  [*] --> SEALED : page indexed on document drop

  SEALED --> REQUESTED : agent calls request_disclosure<br/>with a stated reason
  REQUESTED --> RELEASED : HUMAN approves in the queue
  REQUESTED --> DENIED : HUMAN denies
  DENIED --> REQUESTED : one re-request permitted
  DENIED --> BLOCKED : second attempt refused for the session
  RELEASED --> SEALED : page reload · session end

  note right of SEALED
    read_snippet → PERMISSION_REQUIRED
    attach_evidence → BOUNDARY_VIOLATION
    locate_evidence → still works
    the agent can see it exists
  end note

  note right of RELEASED
    read_snippet returns text
    capped 1200 chars · delimited
    untrustedContentHint set
    LedgerEntry written
  end note

  note right of DENIED
    read_snippet → PERMISSION_DENIED
    hint: do not re-request
    LedgerEntry written for the denial too
  end note

  note left of REQUESTED
    THE ONLY TRANSITION TO RELEASED
    is called from one place in the codebase:
    the approval card click handler.
    No tool execute can reach it.
  end note
